set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

/-!
# Resolution of monomial marked ideals (`N = M`)

Parts (2)
and (3) of the monomial case for `N = M`; the ambient case of the monomial blowup at the maximum locus.  Sources:
Włodarczyk 2005, Step 2b of the proof of the resolution theorem (blow up the intersection of a minimal set of members
whose exponents add up to the mark; the invariant drops); Bierstone--Milman 2008, §5 (the monomial case).

Let `(X, X, E, 𝔞, d)` be a well-formed marked ideal whose ideal is monomial (`𝓜(𝔞) ⊆ 𝔞`) and nonzero at every point,
`γ = MonomialCase.gamma` its invariant, `C` the maximum locus of `γ` on the cosupport (an admissible centre,
`MonomialCase.isAdmissibleCentre_maxLocus_gamma`) and `π : Y → X` the blowup along `C`.

* `IsPrincipalAt 𝔞 E z a`: the stalk at `z` (hence, for a coherent ideal, every stalk near `z`) is generated by the
  monomial `∏_{z ∈ E_i} u_{σ i}^{a_i}` in centred coordinates `u` in which the members through `z` are the
  hyperplanes `{u_{σ i} = 0}`; then `𝔞` is nonzero and monomial at `z` and `γ(z)` is read off `a`
  (`IsPrincipalAt.isNonzeroAt`, `.monomialPart_le`, `.gamma_eq`);
* `isPrincipalAt_of_monomial`: a monomial ideal is principal in this sense at every point, with the exponents
  `e_{E_i}(x)` (`DivisorExponent.divExp`);
* off the centre: `exists_chart_comp` (a flat chart at `π z` read through `π`), `geoTransform_mem_iff_pullback`
  (the transformed ideal is the pullback), `isPrincipalAt_geoTransform_of_notMem` (the transform is principal at `z`,
  with the exponents of `π z`), so `γ'(z) = γ(π z)` (`gamma_geoTransform_eq_of_notMem`);
* the maximum locus `maxLocusγ` near one of its points `x`: a level set of `γ` (`mem_maxLocusγ_iff`), the intersection
  of the members of the top set `I` of `γ(x)` (`eventually_mem_maxLocusγ_iff`), and the members containing it near `x`
  are exactly those of `I` (`filter_eventually_subset_eq_topIdx`, by a curve leaving one coordinate hyperplane);
* over the centre: this and `MonomialBlowup.exists_snc_chart_geoTransform_of_flat` give
  `isPrincipalAt_geoTransform_of_mem` (principal at `z`, exceptional exponent `∑_I a - d`); with
  `BoundaryCount.card_filter_mem_geoStrictTransform_lt` (some member of the top set has strict transform missing `z`)
  and `MonomialInvariant.inv_lt_of_blowup`, `gamma_geoTransform_lt_of_mem`: `γ'(z) < γ(π z)`;
* `monomial_step`: the transform is again well formed with `N = M`, monomial and nonzero everywhere, and `γ'` on the
  new cosupport is below the maximum of `γ` (the monomial case (2));
* `towerInv`, `invariants_canonicalSegment`: the invariant at the stages of towers, and the hypotheses persist along
  canonical segments;
* `exists_isGeoResolution_of_monomial`: over a compact base, iterating the blowup of the maximum locus of `γ` resolves
  `(X, X, E, 𝔞, d)` for `d ≥ 1` (the monomial case (3), via
  `ResolutionDriver.exists_isGeoResolution_of_wellFounded_invariant`).

This module does not import, even transitively,
`AnalyticGeometry.RelativePrincipalization` or `AnalyticGeometry.EmbeddedResolution`.
-/

open Set Filter Finset
